    "number": "Theorem 2",
    "quote": "For the contextual bandit problem with linear payoff functions, for any number of trials T and K actions (where T \\ge K \\ge 2), for any any algorithm A choosing action a_t at time t, there is a constant \\gamma > 0, for d^2 \\le T a sequence of d-dimensional vectors x_{t,a}, such that E[\\sum_t \\max x_{t,a}^T\\theta^* - \\sum_t r_{t,a_t}] \\ge \\gamma\\sqrt{Td}."
